   <div class="window-body has-space">
    <ul class="tree-view has-collapse-button has-connector has-container">
  <details open>
    <summary><a href="/blog/posts/blog1/">Do you need dysphoria to be trans?</a></summary>
    <ul>
      <li>As a trans person 5 years on t, post top surgey, with severe dysphoria...I truly do not think it matters. Transmedicalism involves a fixation on non dysphoric trans people that is not mirrored by real life obstacles that trans people face. If I am pro trans, I will not push the idea that being trans requires gender dysphoria, a mental illness. No one gets a say in the gender identity assigned to them at birth, everyone should have the autonomy to decide whether or not they want to maintain that identity.

</ul>
